# Human's Moonlight Syndrome (SLPS-01001): 16-bit codes, stored high byte first (00 50 = あ).
# What every chapter shares, read from the kana sheet on the discs (entry 1 of each chapter archive, the same
# bitmaps in all twelve): punctuation 0x00-0x09, digits 0x10-0x19, Latin letters 0x1A-0x4D, then hiragana 0x50-0x9F
# and katakana 0xA0-0xEF in gojuon order. 0x0A-0x0F and 0x4E-0x4F are blank cells.
# Kanji are 0x0100 up and numbered anew by each chapter: one of tables/ps1/SLPS-01001-<chapter>.tbl goes after this
# file (named after the chapter archives: prologue, henlin, henshits, mowdei, sowguw on disc 1; denpow, dowaku,
# epilogue, fuyou, hamon, kaibyo, shitsow on disc 2).
# Control words (in the entry's `controls`): FFFF ends a text, FFFD breaks the line, FFFC ends the page. FFF9 and
# FFFA are followed by one more word, a count of frames (FFF9 012C waits for a press, FFFA 0008 pauses). FFFE
# is a gap in the row, half a character wide (the pen moves 8 dots and nothing is drawn): a space here.
# (Twilight Syndrome uses a different layout: tables/ps1/SLPS-00102.tbl.)
